type":"decks.ink","tool":"pen","color":"ink","size":4,"points":[5.6,10.7,0.5,4.6,10,0.5,9.5,9.7,0.5,34.2,10.7,0.5,31.4,15,0.5,30.9,17.8,0.5,33.5,19.5,0.5,38.3,19.5,0.5,41.1,18,0.5,43.2,15.4,0.5,44.5,11.1,0.5,43.7,8.8,0.5,42.2,7.2,0.5,37.9,4.7,0.5,35.6,4.7,0.5,35.1,5.7,0.5,40.8,8.7,0.5,59.6,14.9,0.5,64.2,16.9,0.5,66,18.4,0.5,66.2,19.4,0.5,66.2,20.4,0.5,64.2,24,0.5,70.8,23.5,0.5,76.5,21.2,0.5,79.5,18.6,0.5,81.6,14.5,0.5,81.6,13.2,0.5,80.6,11.2,0.5,78.1,9.9,0.5,70.5,9.6,0.5,67.7,10.6,0.5,67.2,11.4,0.5]}},{"type":"path","id":"1lD82","name":"Ink","x":10725,"y":138325,"width":27,"height":30,"viewBox":[0,0,27,30],"geometry":"M5.8 24.8Q4.5 12 4.7 10.4Q4.8 8.7 5.6 7.7Q6.3 6.7 7.6 5.8Q8.9 4.9 10.4 4.5Q11.9 4.1 13.5 4.1Q15 4.1 16.7 4.8Q18.3 5.4 19.7 6.7Q21.1 7.9 21.7 9.4Q22.2 10.9 22.2 12.6Q22.2 14.2 21.7 15.5Q21.2 16.7 17.9 21L14.6 25.3","stroke":"$decks-ink","strokeWidth":4,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","metadata":{"type":"decks.ink","tool":"pen","color":"ink","size":4,"points":[5.8,24.8,0.5,4.5,12,0.5,4.8,8.7,0.5,6.3,6.7,0.5,8.9,4.9,0.5,11.9,4.1,0.5,15,4.1,0.5,18.3,5.4,0.5,21.1,7.9,0.5,22.2,10.9,0.5,22.2,14.2,0.5,21.2,16.7,0.5,14.6,25.3,0.5]}},{"type":"path","id":"fAAx6","name":"Ink","x":10739,"y":138363,"width":11,"height":13,"viewBox":[0,0,11,13],"geometry":"M4.7 4.6L6.5 8.9","stroke":"$decks-ink","strokeWidth":4,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","metadata":{"type":"decks.ink","tool":"pen","color":"ink","size":4,"points":[4.7,4.6,0.5,6.5,8.9,0.5]}},{"type":"text","id":"outline2-title","content":"Revised outline, from your notes (yellow = changed or new)","fontSize":40,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#6b7280","x":7869,"y":138620},{"type":"frame","id":"outline2","layout":"horizontal","gap":28,"alignItems":"start","children":[{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c0","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c0-h","content":"Cold open","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#6b7280","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c0-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**0:00** A robot lost in a Minecraft maze hunts for cake, with zombies and skeletons waiting in the dark"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c0-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**0:50** The maze becomes an MDP. Each room is a **state**, each move an **action**, and cake (+10) and zombie (−10) are **rewards**"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c0-p2","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"The long title folds into its letters: **MDP**"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c1","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c1-h","content":"The goal, and why brute force fails","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#6b7280","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c1-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"A **policy** picks an action in every state, and finding the best one is the goal"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c1-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"The obvious try: test all 4^7 = **16,384** policies and keep the best","fill":"#FFF1B8"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c1-p2","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"It doesn't scale: chess has about 10^44 states, Go 10^170. And it's wasteful: near-identical policies judged from scratch","fill":"#FFF1B8"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c1-p3","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**So we need cleverer ways**, in two groups: Part 1 knows the MDP's rules, the state transition probabilities (**model-based**), Part 2 doesn't (**model-free**)","fill":"#FFF1B8"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c2","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c2-h","content":"Part 1 · Policy iteration (new)","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#3b82f6","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c2-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"The **model**: where each action leads (**transitions**) and what it pays. Picture it as the map, once, then call it the model","fill":"#FFF1B8"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c2-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**Value** V(s): the reward you can expect from a state, with each step discounted by γ = 0.9","fill":"#FFF1B8"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c2-p2","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**Policy evaluation** computes V(s) under the policy from the model; **policy improvement** switches each state to its best action. Repeat","fill":"#FFF1B8"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c3","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c3-h","content":"Part 1 · Value iteration","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#3b82f6","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c3-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**Bellman equation**: V(s) = the best action's reward + γ × V(next state)"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c3-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"No separate evaluation: the max folds improvement into every update","fill":"#FFF1B8"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c3-p2","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"Apply it to every state, one **sweep** at a time: 10, 9, 8.1… converged in 4 sweeps"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c3-p3","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"The **greedy policy** takes the highest-value action in each state. Both Part 1 methods need the model (and the robot eats the cake)","fill":"#FFF1B8"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c4","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c4-h","content":"Part 2 · Monte Carlo","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#e8590c","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c4-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"Drop the model. Why it matters: cars, robot hands and language models can't know their transitions in advance"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c4-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"The fog: from the start state, 1 time in 4 the zombie steps up. The **transition** is random, and the agent isn't told the odds"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c4-p2","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"Play whole **episodes** and average their discounted **returns**: 5.9, −8.1, 7.29…"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c4-p3","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"Evaluate, improve, repeat: **policy iteration from Part 1**, with sampled returns in place of the model. But it waits for each episode to end","fill":"#FFF1B8"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c5","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c5-h","content":"Part 2 · TD and Q-learning","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#e8590c","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c5-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**TD**: after each step, move V(s) toward r + γ V(s′), the **TD target**"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c5-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"With a learning rate of ½, one update from 0 toward 10 gives 5. Estimates **bootstrap** from estimates, outward from the cake"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c5-p2","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"Up from the start has two next states: ¾ the empty one (8.1), ¼ the **terminal** zombie state (−10). So Q(s, up) is about 3, Q(s, right) about 7"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c5-p3","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**Q-learning**: move Q(s, a) toward r + γ max Q(s′, a′). The max makes it **value iteration from Part 1** without the model (Watkins, 1989)","fill":"#FFF1B8"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c6","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c6-h","content":"The family","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#6b7280","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c6-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"The two-by-two: model-based or model-free, down; policy iteration or value iteration, across. MC and TD sit under PI, Q-learning under VI","fill":"#FFF1B8"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c6-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"Every method searches for the **optimal policy**, learning from the gap between expected and received reward"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c6-p2","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"**All modern AI learns this way.** Maybe we do too?","fill":"#FFF1B8"}]},{"type":"frame","id":"ol2-c7","layout":"vertical","gap":14,"width":300,"children":[{"type":"text","id":"ol2-c7-h","content":"Coda","fontSize":22,"fontWeight":"700","fill":"#d92e3c","textGrowth":"fixed-width","width":300},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c7-p0","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"Blackout, glowing eyes, lightning: **Herobrine** on a hill with an enchanted diamond sword"},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-c7-p1","width":300,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"content":"“Learn… or die.” Glitch, then black"}]}],"x":7869,"y":138700},{"type":"note","id":"ol2-vocab","width":320,"metadata":{"type":"decks.markdown"},"fill":"#DCEBFF","content":"### The words step up\n\nPlain words in the cold open, MDP terms from then on:\n\n| early | later |\n|---|---|\n| room, square | state |\n| move | action |\n| the map | the model, transitions |\n| a trip | an episode |\n| what it earned | the return |\n| a guess | an estimate, V(s), Q(s, a) |\n| the zombie square | a terminal state |","x":7509,"y":138700},{"type":"path","id":"m8Vbw","name":"Ink","x":8426,"y":138983,"width":406,"height":150,"viewBox":[0,0,406,150],"geometry":"M382.5 53.5Q385.5 50.4 385.8 48.8Q386 47.3 385.6 46.5Q385.2 45.6 382.7 43.2Q380.2 40.7 373.7 36.6Q367.2 32.4 357.2 28Q347.1 23.6 337.4 20.3Q327.7 16.